00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:07,098
CHAPTER 5. a device from a Caterpillar The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each

2
00:00:07,099 --> 00:00:12,138
other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the hookah

3
00:00:12,139 --> 00:00:17,479
out of its mouth, and addressed her in a language sleepy voice.

4
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:21,919
“Who are you?

5
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,018
said the Caterpillar.

6
00:00:24,019 --> 00:00:28,098
This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation.

7
00:00:28,099 --> 00:00:34,999
Alice replied, rather shyly, “I— —I hardly know, sir, just at present— —at least I know

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,578
who I was when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several

9
00:00:40,579 --> 00:00:48,678
times since then.” “What do you mean by that?” said the Caterpillar sternly. “Explain yourself!”

10
00:00:48,679 --> 00:00:54,799
“I can’t explain myself I’m afraid, sir,” said Alice, “because I’m not myself, you see.”

11
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:59,238
“I don’t see,” said the Caterpillar.

12
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:04,999
“I’m afraid I can’t put it more clearly,” Alice replied very politely, “for I can’t

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,439
understand it myself to begin with; and being so many different sizes in a day

14
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:14,238
is very confusing.” “It isn’t,” said the Caterpillar.

15
00:01:14,239 --> 00:01:18,857
“Well, perhaps you haven’t found it so yet,” said Alice; “but when you have to turn

16
00:01:18,858 --> 00:01:23,058
into a chrysalis— —you will someday you know— —and then after that into a

17
00:01:23,059 --> 00:01:29,058
butterfly, I should think you’ll feel it a little queer, won’t you?” “Not a bit,”

18
00:01:29,059 --> 00:01:31,038
said the Caterpillar.

19
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:35,178
“Well, perhaps your feelings may be different,” said Alice; “all I know is, it

20
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:43,879
would feel very queer to me “You!” said the Caterpillar contemptuously. “Who are you?

21
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:48,499
Which brought them back again to the beginning of the conversation. Alice felt

22
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:52,879
a little irritated at the caterpillars making such very short remarks, and she

23
00:01:52,880 --> 00:02:01,000
