24
00:02:01,219 --> 00:02:04,999
“Why?” said the Caterpillar.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,317
Here was another puzzling question; and as Alice could not think of any good

26
00:02:09,318 --> 00:02:13,779
reason, and as the Caterpillar seemed to be in a very unpleasant state of mind,

27
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:19,038
she turned away. “Come back!” the Caterpillar called after her I have

28
00:02:19,039 --> 00:02:23,598
something important to say!” This sounded promising, certainly:

29
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:27,018
Alice turned and came back again.

30
00:02:27,019 --> 00:02:31,879
“Keep your temper,” said the Caterpillar.

31
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:37,098
“Is that all?” said Alice, swallowing down her anger as well as she could.

32
00:02:37,099 --> 00:02:40,279
“No,” said the Caterpillar.

33
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:44,479
Alice thought she might as well wait, as she had nothing else to do, and perhaps

34
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:47,658
after all it might tell her something worth hearing.

35
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:52,879
For some minutes it puffed away without speaking, but at last it unfolded its

36
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:57,499
arms, took the hookah out of its mouth again, and said,

37
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:02,118
“So you think you’re changed, do you?”

38
00:03:02,119 --> 00:03:05,238
“I’m afraid I am, sir,” said Alice; “I can’t

39
00:03:05,239 --> 00:03:10,279
remember things as I used— —and I don’t keep the same size for 10 minutes together!”

40
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:15,138
“Can’t remember what things?” said the Caterpillar.

41
00:03:15,139 --> 00:03:19,638
“Well, I’ve tried to say “How doth the little busy bee,” but it all came out

42
00:03:19,639 --> 00:03:25,817
different!” Alice replied in a very melancholy voice. “Repeat, You are old,

43
00:03:25,818 --> 00:03:29,178
Father William said the Caterpillar.

44
00:03:29,179 --> 00:03:34,939
Alice folded her hands, and began:— “You are old, Father William,” the young man

45
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:40,578
said, “And your hair has become very white; And yet you incessantly stand on your

46
00:03:40,579 --> 00:03:46,218
head— Do you think, at your age, it is right?” “In my youth,” Father William replied to

47
00:03:46,219 --> 00:03:51,379
his son, “I feared it might injure the brain; But, now that I’m perfectly sure I

48
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:57,018
have none, Why, I do it again and again.” “You are old,” said the youth, “as I

49
00:03:57,019 --> 00:04:03,259
mentioned before, And have grown most uncommonly fat; Yet you turned a back somersault in at

50
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:06,439
the door— Pray, what is the reason of that?”

51
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:11,479
“In my youths at the sage, as he shook his gray locks, “I kept all my limbs very

52
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:18,138
supple By the use of this ointment— —one shilling the box— Allow me to sell you a couple?”

53
00:04:18,139 --> 00:04:22,578
“You are old,” said the youth, “and your jaws are too weak For anything tougher than

54
00:04:22,579 --> 00:04:27,379
suet; Yet you finished the goose, with the bones and the beak— Pray, how did you

55
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:32,479
manage to do it?” “In my youths at his father, “I took to the law, And argued each

56
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:36,979
case with my wife; And the muscular strength, which it gave to my jaw, Has

57
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:41,899
lasted the rest of my life.” “You are old,” said the youth, “one would hardly suppose

58
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:47,299
That your eye was as steady as ever; Yet you balanced an eel on the end of your

59
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:52,939
nose— What made you so awfully clever?” “I have answered three questions, and that

60
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:57,618
is enough,” Said his father; “don’t give yourself heirs Do you think I can listen

61
00:04:57,619 --> 00:05:02,598
all day to such stuff? Be off, or I’ll kick you downstairs

62
00:05:02,599 --> 00:05:07,279
That has not said right,” said the Caterpillar.

63
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:12,558
“Not quite right, I’m afraid,” said Alice, timidly; “some of the words have got

64
00:05:12,559 --> 00:05:18,198
altered.” “It is wrong from beginning to end,” said the Caterpillar decidedly, and

65
00:05:18,199 --> 00:05:20,959
there was silence for some minutes.

66
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:24,439
The Caterpillar was the first to speak.

67
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:31,399
“What size do you want to be he said Oh, I’m not particular as to size,” Alice

68
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:37,999
hastily replied; “only one doesn’t like changing so often, you know.” “I don’t know,”

69
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,799
said the Caterpillar.

70
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:44,899
Alice said nothing she'd never been so much contradicted in her life before, and

71
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:48,018
she felt that she was losing her temper.

72
00:05:48,019 --> 00:05:52,098
“Are you content now?” said the Caterpillar.

73
00:05:52,099 --> 00:05:56,959
“Well, I should like to be a little larger, sir, if you wouldn’t mind,” said Alice:

74
00:05:56,960 --> 00:06:03,919
“three inches is such a wretched height to be.” “It is a very good height indeed!” said the

75
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:11,058
Caterpillar angrily, rearing itself upright as it spoke (it was exactly three inches high).

76
00:06:11,059 --> 00:06:16,578
“But I’m not used to it!” pleaded poor Alice in a piteous tone. And she thought

77
00:06:16,579 --> 00:06:21,259
of herself, “I wish the creatures wouldn’t be so easily offended!”

78
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:25,879
“You’ll get used to it in time,” said the Caterpillar; and it put the hookah into

79
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,999
its mouth and began smoking again.

80
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,078
This time Alice waited patiently until it chose to speak again.

81
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:36,919
In a minute or two the Caterpillar took the hookah out of its mouth and yawned

82
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:39,078
